-- title:
--   Common width along both degeneracy legs of the ℓ-roof
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $p$ with $5 \le p$ and an algebraically closed field $K$ of characteristic $p$ with decidable equality, together with natural numbers $N \neq 0$ and $\ell$ prime, subject to $(N : K) \neq 0$, $\ell \nmid N$ and $\ell \neq p$. Let $\alpha =$ `heckeAlphaC K N ℓ` be the inclusion of `modularFunctionFieldC K N` into the roof `charLDegeneracyRoof K N ℓ`, the $K$-subfield of $K((q))$ generated by $j(q)$, $j(q^N)$, $j(q^\ell)$ and $j(q^{N\ell})$, and let $\beta =$ `heckeBetaC K N ℓ` be the $K$-algebra map into the same roof induced by the substitution $q \mapsto q^{\ell}$; both are assumed to have integral underlying ring homomorphisms, with witnesses $h\alpha$, $h\beta$. Let $y$ be a place of the roof, i.e. a proper valuation subring containing the image of $K$ and a principal ideal ring, and assume its restriction $y_\alpha$ along $\alpha$ (the pullback valuation subring) satisfies the supersingularity predicate `ssPlaces p N K`. Then there exists $w \in \mathbb{N}$ with $1 \le w$ such that $e_\alpha(y)\,w =$ `placeWidth N` $(y_\alpha)$ and $e_\beta(y)\,w =$ `placeWidth N` $(y_\beta)$, where $e_\varphi(y)$ is the least positive $n$ of the form $\mathrm{ord}_y(\varphi f)$ with $f \neq 0$, and `placeWidth N w` is $\mathrm{jWidth}$ of the residue value of the generator $j$ at $w$ (namely $3$, $2$ or $1$ according as that value is $0$, $1728$ or neither) divided by `placeRamificationJ N w`.
--
--   This is the statement that a supersingular point of the roof has a single intrinsic stacky width, read off consistently through both degeneracy maps $\alpha, \beta : X_0(N) \leftarrow X_0(N\ell)$; the two displayed identities are the ramification-times-width relations on the two legs. It supplies the width hypotheses used in the analysis of the supersingular Hecke operator, and is cited in the computation of the order of the Hecke multiplier on fibres.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_exists_ramificationIndexAlong_mul_eq_placeWidth_restrictAlong_heckeAlphaC_heckeBetaC.lean

